.TH REGEX 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
Regex \- regular expression matching, search, and replacement
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B Regex
module provides ECMAScript-syntax regular expressions via C++ std::regex.
The subject argument may be a
.B string()
or an open
.B file()
(the whole file is read).
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS match
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
bool() match(pattern: string(), subject: string()|file())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns true if the
.I entire
subject matches the pattern (std::regex_match).
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBRuntimeError\fR (bad regex)
.SS search
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
list() search(pattern: string(), subject: string()|file())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Finds the first match.  Returns a list: [full_match, group1, group2, ...].
Returns [] if no match.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBRuntimeError\fR (bad regex)
.SS find_all
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
list() find_all(pattern: string(), subject: string()|file())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns a list of all non-overlapping full matches.  Capture groups are not
included in the result list.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBRuntimeError\fR (bad regex)
.SS replace
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
string() replace(pattern, subject, replacement: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Replaces all occurrences of pattern in subject with replacement.
ECMAScript replacement syntax ($1, $2, ...) is supported.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBRuntimeError\fR (bad regex)
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Json(3), FileStream(3)
